Z||000003||stimpy||07-18-2001||10:20 PM||||Could be illegal, but I would think that you would look behind you for cops before you start backing up.<P>If you want to change bulbs (for any reason), pop the black tabs that run along the edge behind the truk, and unscrew the long bolts underneath. The bulb assembly will seperate from the housing with a quarter turn. You should be easy from there. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||West Coast Fiero||07-18-2001||10:23 PM||||common sence dictates that blue backup lights are much more noticeable than simply going without a front plate as I am sure many folks in CA do, as we are both from CA I can share experience as far as what is tickitable and what is not. If I were a cop and had to choose between a plate infraction or a civilian with police colored lights, I believe I would have to ticket  the light offender<P><BR> besides, who wants a ticket||||reg||1
